# Real records / PHI — never commit
*.pdf
# ...except the two blank government forms the tool ships with. These are
# public DoD forms containing no personal data (verified: zero filled
# fields), and bundling them is what lets the app run on a machine that
# has never downloaded them.
!forms/*.pdf
# The browser build's copies of those same blank forms, plus its module
# manifest. Both are generated by tools/build_web.py from files already in
# this repo -- they contain no personal data, and the site 404s without them.
!docs/app/forms/*.pdf
!web/forms/*.pdf
!docs/app/py/MANIFEST.txt
# Blanket-ignore .txt because that is what the record artifacts are: raw
# extracted text, page sidecars, PII literal lists. Keeping it broad means a
# future extracted_whatever.txt cannot reach a commit by accident.
#
# The cost is that a NEEDED .txt gets silently dropped instead -- which has
# now happened three times, most recently to requirements.txt, so a commit
# pushed green while CI could not install anything. Every exception below is
# a generated or hand-written file with no personal data in it, and
# tests/test_repo_hygiene.py fails if one of them stops being tracked.
*.txt
!requirements.txt
!forms/FORM_VERSIONS.txt
!pii_literals.example.txt
!tools/sample_record.txt
conditions.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Real extracted output — contains actual condition/diagnosis data
conditions_worksheet.md

# Page-offset sidecars — filename embeds the source document name (which
# embeds the member's name), so gitignored alongside the records themselves
*.pages.json

# Pipeline outputs derived from real conditions/PHI
proposals.json
confirmed.json
*_FILLED.pdf

# Your real literal PII values for pii_scrub.py -- never commit this
pii_literals.txt

# Raw OCR output -- full recognized text from the scanned record
ocr_output.json

# Reconciliation output -- cites real conditions and record pages
reconciliation.json


# --- Extra safety for anyone who forks this ---
# Outputs derived from real records. Broad on purpose: a false negative here
# means someone's medical data in a public repo.
*_FILLED*.pdf
*VSO_package*.zip
ocr_output*.json
reconciliation*.json
questions_to_check.md
evidence_index.md
work/
uploads/
records/
